  should have known about sooner. Who is that person, and what did they miss?

  Some shapes that moment commonly takes, to react against rather than to pick from:

  - [1mA teammate reassigned work to you[0m and you found out days late — the pain is [3mhandoffs[0m, and the fix is targeted at
    assignment, not at all changes.
  - [1mA task you depend on got blocked or slipped[0m — the pain is [3mdependencies[0m, and "care about" means something closer to
    watching than owning.
  - [1mSomething's on fire and nobody noticed[0m — the pain is [3murgency[0m, and the real fix might be escalation rules rather than
    a notification feed.
  - [1mYou forgot your own deadline[0m — the pain is [3mmemory[0m, and this is the single-user reminder version with no
    collaboration underneath it.

  These pull in genuinely different directions. The handoff version can be quite small: a couple of event types and an
  in-app inbox. The dependency version needs a watch/subscribe model and a task graph. The urgency version is mostly
  about rules and delivery channels, not about the event log.

  If none of those fits, describing the situation in your own words is better than picking the closest one.
